---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="AI visibility" description="How Evidentia measures brand visibility in AI answer engines: versioned query sets, paraphrases, repeated sampling through official provider APIs, Wilson score intervals, per-model and per-intent breakdowns, and series breaks on model-version changes." path="/ai-visibility" pageType="TechArticle" breadcrumbs={[{ name: 'AI visibility', path: '/ai-visibility' }]}>
  <section class="hero wrap">
    <span class="eyebrow">Observatory</span>
    <h1>One AI answer is an anecdote. Thirty-two, with an interval, is a measurement.</h1>
    <p class="lede">Generative answers are stochastic: resampling the same prompt explains about a third of the variance in whether a brand appears, and the query language explains another quarter. Evidentia's observatory is built for that reality.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="block"><div class="wrap">
    <div class="bento">
      <div class="card wide"><span class="n">PROTOCOL</span><h3>Repeats × paraphrases × models × language × date</h3><p>Query sets are versioned. Each query carries an intent, a branded/unbranded flag and paraphrases. Each cell is sampled repeatedly (8 by default) through the provider's official API. Rates are reported with 95% Wilson score intervals and the sample size; a change is only called significant when a two-proportion test says so.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><span class="n">TRACKED</span><h3>Per observation</h3><ul><li>brand mention (word-boundary, aliases)</li><li>citation of your domains</li><li>competitor mentions and first-mention order</li><li>provider, model, model version, retrieval mode</li><li>language, geography, sample index, timestamp</li><li>answer hash — not the answer text</li></ul></div>
      <div class="card"><span class="n">SERIES BREAKS</span><h3>Model versions change</h3><p>When a provider silently updates a model, the report marks a break in the series instead of smoothing over it.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><span class="n">TERMS</span><h3>Official APIs only</h3><p>Every major provider's consumer terms prohibit automated access to the chat interface. Evidentia calls the Anthropic Messages API, OpenAI-compatible Chat Completions (including Perplexity's Sonar models) and the Gemini API, parsing whichever citation format each provider returns, and stores aggregates where terms restrict link-level monitoring.</p></div>
      <div class="card ink"><span class="n">HONESTY</span><h3>n = 32 gives ±17 points at 50%.</h3><p>Detecting a 10-point change needs roughly 100 samples per cell. The console shows the interval next to every number so nobody reads noise as trend.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div></section>
  <section class="block"><div class="wrap prose">
    <h2>Reading a report</h2>
<pre is:raw tabindex="0"><code>northwind-reconciliation-be v2 — 224 observations (2026-09-01 → 2026-09-15)
Overall mention 46% [39–53] n=224, citation 21% [16–27] n=224

Per model:
  mistral/mistral-large-latest: mention 51% [42–60], citation 24% [17–33]
  anthropic/claude-x:           mention 41% [32–50], citation 19% [12–27]

Per query:
  q1 (commercial) …: mention 63% [49–75], citation 31% [20–45], avg position 1.4
  q3 (navigational, branded) …: mention 97% [84–100], citation 44% [29–60]

Series breaks (model version changed): anthropic/claude-x: 2026-08 → 2026-09</code></pre>
    <p>Mention and citation behave differently by engine — some cite without naming, others name without citing — so both are always shown. Branded prompts are reported separately from unbranded ones.</p>
    <h2>What it is not</h2>
    <ul><li>Not a rank tracker: there is no stable "position 1" in generative answers.</li><li>Not a scraper: no consumer UI automation, no headless browsers against providers.</li><li>Not a promise: visibility depends on retrievability, evidence and off-site presence; the observatory tells you where you stand and whether a change was real.</li></ul>
  </div></section>
</Base>
